# Design System — read `/design.md` before UI edits

The project has a locked editorial design system at `/design.md` at the
repo root. All UI changes — new components, redesigns, style edits — must
honour it. Two reasons it matters: (1) the system was authored after a
Hallmark audit found 50 design tells across marketing, app, and conversion
surfaces, and the file encodes the fixes as rules; (2) page-level theme
or macrostructure improvisation is **banned** on this project — pages within
a family must share the system, not drift from it.

When editing UI code, read `/design.md` for the full contract. The
non-negotiables, summarised:

## Tokens
- Every colour references a named token. Never inline `#hex`, `oklch()`,
  `rgb()`, or Tailwind palette colours like `emerald-500`, `rose-400`,
  `amber-100`.
- Amber transparency uses **only** `--amber-wash` (0.04), `--amber-tint`
  (0.10), or `--amber-emphasis` (0.20). No `amber/[0.05]` improvisation.
- Status colours use `--color-status-positive` · `attention` · `risk`.

## Type
- Fraunces (display) + Inter (body) + JetBrains Mono. No fourth font.
- Section heads in Fraunces, `tracking-tight`, sentence case.

## Section heads — eyebrows banned by default
- `<Eyebrow>` is **opt-in**, ≤ 2 per page, only for genuinely ordinal /
  contextual data (e.g. dashboard meta-line "Week 12 · Q1 · 2026").
- Never use `<Eyebrow>` as decoration above a section heading.
- Replace uppercase mono-cap labels above headings with the heading alone.

## Components — atoms are locked
- Every input goes through shadcn `<Input>` from `@/components/ui/input`.
  Raw `<input>` is forbidden on auth, onboarding, and any new forms.
- Every primary affordance goes through shadcn `<Button>` from
  `@/components/ui/button`. Raw `<button>` allowed only for icon-only
  inline controls (dismiss-X, action-row buttons).
- Brand marks go through `<BrandMark size="sm|md|xl" />`. The `✦` Unicode
  glyph and literal letter logomarks are deprecated.

## Motion
- Motion-cut everywhere except the onboarding-wizard step transition
  (directional fade, 160ms, `--ease-out`).
- No perpetual ambient motion. No scroll-triggered fade-up. No
  `transition-all`. No `hover:scale-*` on non-clickable surfaces.
- Honour `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Microinteractions
- **Silent success.** No "Saved!" / "Archived!" / "Done!" toasts. Toasts
  only for failures and async actions whose effect isn't visible.
- Reversible destructive actions get an Undo toast (7s), never a
  confirmation modal.

## Card-in-card
- One containment layer per surface. Don't wrap a `<Card>` around a row of
  bordered items that already look card-shaped.

## Anti-patterns (auto-fail on review)
- Centered-card-on-empty-viewport auth/onboarding shells
- 3-equal feature grids with icon-tile-above-heading-above-2-lines
- Aurora-blob / mandala-wash decorative backgrounds (the mandala lives
  only as `<BrandMark />` now)
- Gradient-fill headlines (`bg-clip-text` with a linear gradient)
- Invented metrics ("10× faster", "50,000+ teams")

Stamp every file you redesign with:
`/* Hallmark · design-system: design.md · designed-as-app */`
